# Existing unnumbered DDL and ownership

This release introduces NO new DDL file and NO formal migration.
The two files in existing-ddl/ are byte-identical copies of the already
accepted main's scheduling/testdata/quota.sql and reservations.sql.
They are existing unnumbered candidates, not an installed catalog.
Accepted base f7842492 is schema 60 / 120 tables and has no scheduling tables.
The earlier schema-59 evidence remains pinned to f726e56b.

ARC owns their eventual contiguous formal migration, scope enumeration,
fresh/restored fingerprints, runtime role grants and readiness admission.
The files add two tables. Apply quota.sql then reservations.sql only after
ARC reconciles the current GW-120/DAT-101/metering queue and assigns the
actual next number. Never renumber accepted lineage or reuse old fingerprints.

scheduling_quota_policy is global: singleton, positive bigint revision and
allocation JSON. scheduling_reservations is cell-owned, with exact attempt,
server tenant/workspace, local site/cell, normalized demand, quota revision
and reserve/release times. Its foreign keys require the installed workspaces
(tenant_id,id) key and site/cell registries; defaults use local_site_id() and
local_cell_id(). Both are required for this reader. Optional borrowing DDL
is separate, remains disabled by default and is not introduced here.

Reuse the current Control business principal and installed Workspace authority.
The reader needs SELECT on both tables and the policy FOR SHARE fence also
requires UPDATE privilege on at least one policy column. PostgreSQL documents
that rule at https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-select.html .
Preserve the identity/Workspace owner's existing row-lock and function grants.
Browser roles get no DB principal or direct table access.

The module enforces audience, current server actor/session/source and Workspace
scope in code. The existing authority allows current members, including viewers,
to read their own allocation; Admin uses its current platform-admin session
within the installed tenant. No tenant/customer/role is accepted from input.
Missing tables/grants fail as storage errors, never fabricated zero capacity.

The six PG tests run under an isolated fixture principal. Production serving-role
and catalog readiness remain ARC/IAM prerequisites to turning on the route.
There is no entitlement signing code, policy seed, capacity/topology producer
or training-consumer activation in this slice.
